# Colour roles and accessibility

Choose each colour by its job: identity, reading, interaction, state or data. The theme colour changes the look of the interface. It never changes what an error, a success or a chart series means. This page gives the rules behind [Colour](colour.html) and adds no colours of its own.

A theme colour does not put a civica logo inside a home. Project identity and household personalisation are separate.

## Choose colours for the task

| Task | Use |
| --- | --- |
| Select interface colours | [Seven GOV.UK theme colours](colour.html) |
| Identify a chart series | [Stable categorical chart colours](chart-colour.html) |
| Show increasing values or distance from a target | [Quantitative colour scales](chart-colour.html#choose-the-colour-mapping) |
| Show locations and spatial measurements | [Maps and zones](../home-assistant/maps-and-zones.html) |
| Explain a task visually | [Illustration](illustration.html) |

